---
/**
 * Private aged care — the second path, and the other half of the design sample.
 *
 * Written for a different reader from the apartment page. This one is usually
 * an adult child, often at a distance, often after something has happened. They
 * are not browsing. They want to know what the place is actually like, whether
 * their parent would be looked after, and who to ring — in that order, quickly.
 *
 * CLAIMS HELD FOR CONFIRMATION (docs/brief.md). This page repeats only what the
 * live site already publishes, and drops what it cannot support:
 *   - kept: twelve suites, single floor, shared kitchen, registered nurse on
 *     site 24 hours. All currently published; all still need sign-off.
 *   - dropped: "the highest benchmarks in Australia" — an unsupported
 *     superlative — and "high staff-to-resident ratio", which is an adjective
 *     rather than a claim. The ratio goes back in as a number, or not at all.
 *   - rewritten: the Home Care Package funding paragraph. Support at Home
 *     replaced that programme on 1 November 2025, so the old wording would be
 *     wrong. It now says to ask us, which is true whatever the scheme is called.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import EnquiryBand from '../components/EnquiryBand.astro';
import Questions from '../components/Questions.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_HREF } from '../site.ts';

import front from '../images/henley-front-web.jpg';

const household = [
  'Twelve private suites on a single floor',
  'Each with a kitchenette and its own seating',
  'A shared residents’ kitchen at the centre of the house',
  'Common living and outdoor spaces',
  'A registered nurse on site, 24 hours',
];

const questions = [
  {
    q: 'What makes this different from a nursing home?',
    a: 'Size and routine. Twelve suites on one floor is a household rather than a wing, and the day is built around how each resident already lives — when they wake, when they eat, what they do — instead of around a schedule everyone fits into.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can my parent move here from an apartment upstairs?',
    a: 'Yes, and it happens. Care is on the same site, so the move is within one address rather than to a different suburb, and the people they know are still here.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does it cost, and what funding can we use?',
    a: 'It depends on the suite and the care needed, and government funding arrangements changed recently. Call us and we will go through what applies to your situation rather than send you a figure that may not.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can we look around before deciding?',
    a: 'Please do. Come and see the household, meet the nurse on duty, and ask the questions this page has not answered.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Private aged care | The Henley on Broadwater"
  description="A twelve-suite aged care household on a single floor in Southport, with a registered nurse on site and care built around how each resident already lives."
>
  <Hero
    image={front}
    alt="The entrance to The Henley on Broadwater at 70 Marine Parade, Southport"
    heading="Private aged care that keeps you feeling like yourself"
    standfirst="A household of twelve suites in Southport, where the day is built around the people living in it."
  >
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="#enquire">Arrange a visit</a>
      <a class="button button--quiet" href={PHONE_HREF}>Call {PHONE}</a>
    </div>
  </Hero>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="lede">
        Needing care should not mean handing over your life. Early bird or night owl, a
        snack at an odd hour, a lie-in on a Sunday — this is a home, and it fits around
        the person living in it.
      </p>

      <h2>The household</h2>
      <ul>{household.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>

      <p>
        Because it is small, the people caring for your mother or father get to know them
        — what they like, who visits, what a bad day looks like. That is not a feature we
        can list. It is the reason to come and see it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--linen">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>If more care is needed later</h2>
      <p>
        Many residents come to the household from an apartment upstairs. Support can also
        come to an apartment in ten-minute increments, for as long as that is enough. The
        point of one address is that changing how much help you need does not mean
        changing where you live, or who your neighbours are.
      </p>
      <p>
        More about <a href="/supported-living/">support in your own apartment</a> and
        <a href="/luxury-retirement-living/">the apartments</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Questions questions={questions} heading="Questions families ask" ground="paper" />

  <EnquiryBand
    interest="agedCare"
    heading="Come and meet us"
    invitation="Most families want to see the household and talk to whoever is on duty before they decide anything. That is exactly what a visit is for."
    formHeading="Arrange a visit"
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    font: var(--type-title-lg);
    color: var(--color-on-surface);
    max-width: 42ch;
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3xl);
  }
</style>
